  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state received $487M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state logged 2,748 awards with an average award size of $177K, and obligations fell 39.4% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show variability: FY21 totaled $624M, FY22 totaled $1.2B, FY23 totaled $1B, FY24 totaled $1.3B, FY25 totaled $804M, and FY26 totaled $487M. The Department of Defense obligated $198M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $103M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $87.1M in FY2026 to date. KBR WYLE SERVICES, LLC received $65M, FEDERAL CONTRACTING INC received $40.4M, and BLACK HILLS SERVICE COMPANY, LLC received $32.2M in FY2026 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $95.8M, Computer Facilities Management Services accounted for $65.4M, and Electric Power Distribution accounted for $33M in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in South Dakota trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 39.4% year over year in FY2026 to date. Obligations by fiscal year show peaks and troughs: FY21 was $624M, FY22 was $1.2B, FY23 was $1B, FY24 was $1.3B, FY25 was $804M, and FY26 was $487M. The current fiscal year total of $487M is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $177K across 2,748 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are largest in South Dakota federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $198M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $103M and the Department of the Interior obligated $87.1M in FY2026 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry with $95.8M, followed by Computer Facilities Management Services with $65.4M and Electric Power Distribution with $33M in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
